  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (2S,3S,4R,5R,6R)-2-methyl-6-[...] and the Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds. Specifically, the compound is linked to RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase, which is a target of trans-Norbixin and 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol. Additionally, the compound is also associated with Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, which is a target of Wikstromol. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may interact with various signaling pathways involving receptor subunits, potentially influencing the function of the Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. The evidence is supported by multiple pathways, suggesting a broad involvement in cellular processes, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
